  "result": "The node can't pass the gate as planned: the first gate run returned `WITNESS_FAIL`, and the cause is in the run's reading rather than in my two files. I used 1 of the 6 gate runs and stopped.\n\n**Why it fails:** the reading lists the electric-scooter aggregate (`DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter`) with **no included class**, and the electric-scooter class itself is only \"unresolved\". Under the aggregate's contract, the check that the subject is an electric scooter is then never true. It comes out unknown for a scooter and false for anything else, so the rule can only ever return unknown or not applicable.\n\nWhat the gate reported:\n- **`forbid`, `permit`, `branch_1`, `branch_2`:** all returned unknown because of the unresolved aggregate, instead of their expected verdicts.\n- **`blind`:** also unknown, but for the aggregate rather than for the masked speed.\n- **`idle`:** passed, because the scooter is on no roadway or bicycle lane, so the rule doesn't apply whatever its class.\n\n**What I wrote:**\n- **Rule:** the subject must be in the electric-scooter aggregate; the rule applies when its footprint overlaps a roadway or a bicycle lane or path; the duty is speed ≤ 15 mph, using the text's own figure. The exception (s1) and \"may be operated\" (s3) are the node's residues, so they aren't written, and I added no narrowings of my own.\n- **Witnesses:** the four planned scenes plus two extras so each place is tested both ways: a bicycle lane at 8 m/s (violated) and a roadway at 5 m/s (compliant).\n\n**Fix for the plan:** in the reading, classify the electric-scooter class as included in `DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter`, and mark the classes the definition leaves out as excluded rather than unresolved. Alternatively, have the node use the electric-scooter class directly if that's allowed. Once the aggregate has an included class, I expect the current rule and witnesses to pass unchanged, but the gate hasn't confirmed that.\n\nOne slip: I ran one shell command other than the gate, a harmless `echo skip`. It changed nothing, and it's noted in the report.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory.",
